Interesting.  I think the shield of reflection is a fairly good
option for knights -- not because I like being stuck with a
shield, but because the other options are worse.  The only
really portable MR-granting artifact for lawfuls is the knight
quest artifact, and the wiki warns quite sternly against
relying on your own quest artifact for MR.  That means
you either need a cloak of MR -- and no robe -- or GDSM.
Assuming you want to wear an amulet of life saving and
a robe, that makes the shield more or less mandatory.

I suppose you could wear a cloak of MR, carry a robe
in a bag of holding, and rely on the mirror for MR
temporarily in non-combat situations when casting
identify and remove curse and whatnot, but you'd
have to give up all hope of ever casting any healing
spells; which would be unfortunate, since knights
can get skill in them.

Although, once you *are* skilled in healing (and
attack spells if you care about those), you could
switch out the shield for the cloak-of-MR, if you
were willing to wish for or spend a scroll on
creating a second type of DSM.  You'd still
need a robe for things like identify, but that's
non-combat.  It's difficult to imagine wanting to
spend resources on a second type of DSM when
you already have one of the really good kinds,
but maybe if you had an unusually large number
of wishes in a particular game, or if you'd found
a stack of extra markers in bones and could
write any number of scrolls of enchant armor,
this might be an option.


